IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-56. NOUNS of the four things this row records: a date printed twice on one line, a reference from one provision to another, an indexation clause, and a power to change a rate.
-- TARGET COMPILER: main. No REFUSE, no section GIVEN, no TYPICALLY, no YMD, no sets: what the sources do not answer is NOTHING from a MAYBE.
--
-- This row is NOT an encoding of the Property Tax and Compensation Fund Law, 5721-1961. It records the references and the dates of four provisions, as typed values the tests check, and keeps each defect as an expected-red test.
-- THE KINDS BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's: each is a short plain description I wrote from reading the citing words and the target, so that two descriptions of the same thing are the same kind.
-- The words of the texts are quoted beside each value in the references module: `src:` lines are the Law's consolidation (an excerpt, deposited), `ext:[...]` lines are typed from a page image of the official instrument.
-- A reference whose two descriptions differ, a date pair that names two days, a clause that leaves a question open, and an instrument of another kind than its power names, are defects, and are kept in an expected-red file.

§ `Nouns of a date printed twice`

-- Only the three Hebrew months the row reads (plus the month of the calendar routine's own control date).
DECLARE `A Hebrew month` IS ONE OF
    `Kislev`
    `Av`
    `Adar I`

-- Where a reading comes from, from the strongest to the weakest.
DECLARE `Where a reading comes from` IS ONE OF
    `the official page, read from its image, and the cropped image is deposited`
    `the official page, read from its image, and the page is not deposited`
    `a search of the official text layer by the row builder, and the issue is not deposited`
    `the consolidation only`
    `the Hebrew-calendar routine, run after its control date`

DECLARE `A date printed on a line` HAS
    `what the line is` IS A STRING
    `the Hebrew day of the month printed` IS A NUMBER
    `the Hebrew month printed` IS A `A Hebrew month`
    `the Hebrew year printed` IS A NUMBER
    `the Gregorian date printed` IS A DATE
    `the day the Hebrew date falls on, by the routine` IS A DATE
    `the printed words were read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `the day by the routine was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

§ `Nouns of a cross-reference`

DECLARE `What a reference points at` IS ONE OF
    `a bimonthly reporting method that another provision of the chapter treats`
    `no bimonthly or one-monthly reporting method in any other provision of the chapter`
    `paragraph (7) of subsection (ב) of s 38לז`
    `paragraphs (1) to (3) of the definition of qualifying expenses in s 38לו`
    `paragraphs (1) to (7) of subsection (ב) of s 38לז`

DECLARE `A cross-reference` HAS
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the citing words say it points at` IS A `What a reference points at`
    `the target is` IS A `What a reference points at`
    `how many things the citing words name` IS A NUMBER
    `how many of them the target has` IS A NUMBER
    `limb (a) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `limb (b) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

§ `Nouns of an indexation clause`

DECLARE `An indexation clause` HAS
    `the clause is in` IS A STRING
    `the day of each year it updates on` IS A STRING
    `the day the instrument that added the clause was published` IS A DATE
    `the first update day after that` IS A DATE
    `the organ the clause names to publish the updated amounts` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `the clause says which amounts a claim for damage before the first update day uses` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the clause was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `the day of publication was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

§ `Nouns of a power to change a rate`

DECLARE `A kind of instrument` IS ONE OF
    `a notice published in Reshumot`
    `regulations published in Kovetz HaTakanot`

DECLARE `A power to change a rate` HAS
    `the power is in` IS A STRING
    `the kind of instrument the power names` IS A `A kind of instrument`
    `the body whose approval the power requires` IS A STRING
    `how many bases the statutory rate is set on` IS A NUMBER
    `the power was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

DECLARE `An instrument made under a power` HAS
    `the instrument is` IS A STRING
    `the kind of the instrument` IS A `A kind of instrument`
    `the body whose approval the instrument recites` IS A STRING
    `the day the instrument was signed` IS A DATE
    `the instrument was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

DECLARE `A rate set for a tax year` HAS
    `the tax year` IS A NUMBER
    `the percentage set` IS A NUMBER
    `how many figures the instrument sets for that tax year` IS A NUMBER
    `the first day of that tax year` IS A DATE
    `the first day was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
